Motor Driver Schematic (textual): motor_driver.kicad_sch

Components:
- U1,U2: TB6612FNG dual H-bridge driver (two drivers for two motors can be one TB6612 per motor or one chip for both motors; TB6612 contains two channels -> use one TB6612 per two motors meaning a single TB6612FNG can drive two motors. We'll use one TB6612FNG for both motors.)
- J1: MOTOR_PWR (2-pin) - BAT+, GND
- J2: M1_OUT (2-pin) - Motor 1 (+ and -)
- J3: M2_OUT (2-pin) - Motor 2 (+ and -)
- J4: CTRL (6-pin) - M1_PWM, M1_DIR, STBY/EN, M2_PWM, M2_DIR, FAULT
- R_sense: series shunt per motor optional for current sense (0.05 ohm) with INA amplifier to report to main board ADC or INA219

Notes:
- TB6612FNG VCC pin supplied from 5V_BCK or 3.3V depending on motor voltage; for 3-6V motors use BAT+ through proper supply or motor driver supply pin
- Include large decoupling capacitors near motor supply and VM pin
- TB6612 requires STBY pin pulled high to enable

Netlist highlights:
- NET VM: motor supply -> J1:BAT+
- NET GND: common
- NET M1_A/M1_B: outputs to J2

Design notes:
- Use wide traces for motor outputs (>=1.5mm)
- Place TB6612 close to motor connectors
